[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two white matte ceramic plates placed side-by-side on an aged oak wood surface with visible grain and small nicks. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view at 40 degrees, ensuring all ingredients on both plates are fully visible and clear. The main foreground plate shows a tender, golden-brown seared pork loin chop placed next to a generous portion of colorful, rustic sides. The pork has a slightly caramelized, dark-brown crust with visible seasoning flecks. Alongside the pork, there is a hearty mix of soft-roasted amber butternut squash cubes, crisp-looking diced apple, and warm, chewy-textured farro leaves coated in a light, glossy mustard-based pan sauce. Deep green baby spinach leaves are partially wilted, intermingled with the grains. The scene is lit by soft natural light from a window to the left, creating gentle shadows and highlighting the sheen of the mustard glaze and natural pork juices. Props include a rumpled beige linen napkin tucked beneath the edge of one plate and a small wooden spoon resting casually on the table nearby. A few scattered sage leaves and a small stray piece of diced apple sit on the wood near the plates. The background is softly blurred with a hint of a kitchen setting. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures an authentic home-cooked meal, warm and inviting. Includes slight natural imperfections: a tiny sauce drip on the rim, uneven browning on the squash, and an asymmetric plating style. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no cold tones. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
]
